---
import { getEntry, render } from 'astro:content';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Quickstart from '../../figures/14-quickstart.astro';

const DOCS = 'https://gitlab.com/dunn.dev/keystone/-/blob/main/docs/';

// docs/setup.md is written for the forge: its h1 is this page's title, and its relative links resolve against docs/ there.
const setup = await getEntry('docs', 'setup');
if (!setup?.rendered) throw new Error('docs/setup.md did not render');
const html = setup.rendered.html
  .replace(/<h1[^>]*>.*?<\/h1>/s, '')
  .replace(/href="(?![a-z]+:|#|\/)([^"]*)"/gi, (_, url) => `href="${new URL(url, DOCS).href}"`);
const headings = (await render(setup)).headings
  .filter(h => h.depth === 2)
  .map(h => ({ slug: h.slug, text: h.text }));
---
<Layout title="Install" description="Install keystone, bind a first disk, rotate, revoke and set up alerts." headings={headings}>
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1 class="page-title">Install</h1>
  </header>
  <div class="cat-explainer figure-pair">
    <Quickstart />
  </div>
  <article>
    <p>The quickstart deploys an empty Worker, confirms it serves no sets, mints a set into the key store and deploys it, which also checks it. The disk is then bound with the thp (the signing key's thumbprint) read from the live advertisement, and the initramfs is rebuilt with network, DNS and a CA bundle so clevis can reach the Worker before the root filesystem mounts. A reboot then unlocks the disk with no passphrase prompt. The numbered steps under Quickstart give each its commands.</p>
    <Fragment set:html={html} />
  </article>
</Layout>
